  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"page-content\"><section><p><h2>Bold thinking on AGI from the lab that pioneered the field.</h2></p></section><div data-header-trigger=\"header-overlap\"><dmi-article-spotlight data-hydration=\"client:idle\"> <section aria-label=\"Featured articles\"><dmi-card data-aspect-ratio=\"16-9\" data-hydration=\"client:idle\" data-orientation=\"portrait\" data-scale=\"hero\" data-surface=\"surface\" data-variant=\"featured\"> <a data-gtm-param-content-name=\"Essays - Introducing the DeepMind Institute\" data-gtm-event=\"select_content\" data-gtm-param-content-type=\"internal\" data-gtm-param-section-name=\"Essays\" href=\"https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/introducing-the-deepmind-institute/\"> <div><header><h2>Introducing the DeepMind Institute</h2><p data-block-key=\"fnadk\">As we near AGI, we urgently need interdisciplinary thinking to better understand its profound implications for humanity.</p><p>Shane Legg, James Manyika and Demis Hassabis</p></header></div> </a> </dmi-card></section> <section aria-label=\"Recent articles\"><dmi-card data-aspect-ratio=\"16-9\" data-hydration=\"client:idle\" data-orientation=\"landscape\" data-scale=\"standard\" data-surface=\"surface\" data-variant=\"standard\"> <a data-gtm-param-content-name=\"Essays - The case for reasoning transparency\" data-gtm-event=\"select_content\" data-gtm-param-content-type=\"internal\" data-gtm-param-section-name=\"Essays\" href=\"https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/the-case-for-reasoning-transparency/\"> <div><header><h2>The case for reasoning transparency</h2><p data-block-key=\"dilm4\">Reading an AI’s ‘chain of thought’ gives us a window into its reasoning, which we can monitor for scheming and deception. We must strive to keep that window open.</p><p>Rohin Shah and Anca Dragan</p></header></div> </a> </dmi-card><dmi-card data-aspect-ratio=\"16-9\" data-hydration=\"client:idle\" data-orientation=\"landscape\" data-scale=\"standard\" data-surface=\"surface\" data-variant=\"standard\"> <a data-gtm-param-content-name=\"Essays - Economic policy for AGI\" data-gtm-event=\"select_content\" data-gtm-param-content-type=\"internal\" data-gtm-param-section-name=\"Essays\" href=\"https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/economic-policy-for-agi/\"> <div><header><h2>Economic policy for AGI</h2><p data-block-key=\"nvk65\">This essay evaluates eleven policies societies could implement to manage the potential economic disruption arising from increasingly advanced and pervasive AI.</p><p>Julian Jacobs and Alex Imas</p></header></div> </a> </dmi-card><dmi-card data-aspect-ratio=\"16-9\" data-hydration=\"client:idle\" data-orientation=\"landscape\" data-scale=\"standard\" data-surface=\"surface\" data-variant=\"standard\"> <a data-gtm-param-content-name=\"Essays - Principles for a new utopianism\" data-gtm-event=\"select_content\" data-gtm-param-content-type=\"internal\" data-gtm-param-section-name=\"Essays\" href=\"https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/principles-for-a-new-utopianism/\"> <div><header><h2>Principles for a new utopianism</h2><p data-block-key=\"eh1w9\">If AGI is to transform society, we must decide what transformations we want. Learning from the turmoil of the twentieth century, this essay proposes a pragmatic utopianism of humility and hope.</p><p>Stephen Cave</p></header></div> </a> </dmi-card><dmi-card data-aspect-ratio=\"16-9\" data-hydration=\"client:idle\" data-orientation=\"landscape\" data-scale=\"standard\" data-surface=\"surface\" data-variant=\"standard\"> <a data-gtm-param-content-name=\"Essays - A framework for frontier AI and the dawning of a new age\" data-gtm-event=\"select_content\" data-gtm-param-content-type=\"internal\" data-gtm-param-section-name=\"Essays\" href=\"https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/a-framework-for-frontier-ai-and-the-dawning-of-a-new-age/\"> <div><header><h2>A framework for frontier AI and the dawning of a new age</h2><p data-block-key=\"3spp3\">A dynamic approach to testing frontier AI model capabilities that supports innovation and incentivizes responsible behavior. This essay first appeared on X.</p><p>Demis Hassabis</p></header></div> </a> </dmi-card></section> </dmi-article-spotlight></div></div></div>",
